            "acc_id1": "",
            "accordion_heading1": "What is The Pain Triangle?",
            "dsc1": "<p><strong>The Pain Triangle: 3 Causes of Period Cramps</strong></p><p><strong>1. Hormonal Imbalance</strong></p><p>Too much estrogen hormone raises prostaglandin levels - the “cramp messengers” that tell your uterus to contract.</p><p><strong>2. Excess Prostaglandins (Cramp Messengers)</strong><br/>In healthy amounts, prostaglandins help the uterus shed its lining during your period. When levels spike, cramps become more intense and painful.<br/></p><p><strong>3. Micronutrient Gaps</strong><br/>Your body needs nutrients like magnesium, calcium, zinc and vitamin D to stay balanced. Without enough, cramps can hit harder.</p><p><strong>How does monthlies help?</strong></p><p>Painkillers only mask cramps once they’ve started. . monthlies strengthens your foundation by addressing the root causes of <em>The Pain Triangle</em>, supporting a healthier cycle from within.</p><p><br/>90% of women reported a significant improvement in their period pain and cramps after just 60 days using monthlies**.</p>"
          }
        },
